//Constructor:
special method invoked automatically at time of object creation.Used for initialization
-same name as class
-construtor doesnt have a return type
-only called once(automatically at object creation)
-memory allocation hapens when constructor is called

There are three types of constucter
-Non parametrize constructer
-Parametrize constructer
-Copy constructer


in a class there can be more constructer but of dufferent types
typye different ==>construtor overloading=>is an example of polymorphism

this is a special pointer in c++ thats points to the current object
this->prop is same as*(this).prop

COPY CONSTUCTOR
special constructer(default )used to copy properties of one object to anothe

